        <briefdescription>
<para>Estimates the fraction of this reader&apos;s indexed rows expected to match the predicate. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Returns a value in [0, 1], or std::nullopt if no estimate is available. Values outside [0, 1] are also treated as unknown by evaluators. Estimates only guide predicate execution order and must never exclude rows. The default implementation returns std::nullopt. TODO(lisizhuo.lsz): Add selectivity estimates for scalar indexes such as bitmap indexes. </para>
